        {
          "title": "Bauerntarock",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Bauerntarock is an Austrian German Tarok point-trick game for three or four players in which hearts are always trumps."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A farmers tarock member of the German Tarok group related to Bavarian Tarock, Dobbm, and Tapp."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "3-4 players use the table arrangement described for Bauerntarock."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card German-suited pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card German-suited pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal from a 36-card German-suited pack; hearts are permanent trumps and the deal may include contracts such as Hineinschauen or Sumpern."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
